__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.env
state.db
traces/
*.ics
.DS_Store
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# ANY agent home, default or alternate — the DIRECTORY, never a file list. The
# home was renamed .prometheus -> .prometheus (prometheus/config.py: resolve_home), so
# these patterns matched nothing and every home's SOUL.md, usage.jsonl and
# outbox/ became committable. DISCORD_HOME gives the bot its own memory
# (prometheus/gateway/discord.py) and PROMETHEUS_HOME can point it anywhere else,
# so one glob has to cover every home, not just the default one.
# Directory-level on purpose: test_runtime_data_is_ignored.py enumerates the
# artifacts by hand, so listing files loses the day a new one appears. The
# leading slash anchors it at the repo root, which is also what keeps this off
# the prometheus/ package directory.
/.prometheus*/
.env.prerename-bak

# Delegated coding deliverables (dated run folders + auto-run logs)
prometheus_workspace/

# Google OAuth: the client file you download from Cloud Console, and any token
# it produces. Nothing here should ever be committed — belt and braces, because
# the docs used to tell people to drop credentials.json in the repo root.
credentials.json
client_secret*.json
*token*.json
.gcp/

# Disposable design mockups: propose, decide, implement, delete.
docs/proposals/*.html

# DeepEval writes a telemetry file here on every run
.deepeval/

# Local agent tooling. Only launch.json is machine-specific: it hardcodes
# .venv/bin/python (a POSIX path) and an optional tracing extra, so it describes
# the machine that wrote it and nothing else. .claude/skills/ is NOT ignored —
# AGENTS.md and docs/context/maintainers.md send contributors there for the
# new-tool and review-pr workflows.
.claude/launch.json

# built by lab/one-memory-every-agent/build_grok_plugin.py
lab/one-memory-every-agent/grok-plugin/

# board sources for videos stay private (conventions §6); commit PNG screenshots
lab/**/*.excalidraw
!lab/kimi-k3/**/*.excalidraw
!lab/pi-agent/**/*.excalidraw

# evals/hosted_docker/test_image.py plants waku/_c1_context_probe/ inside an
# admitted build-context tree to prove the ignore files keep secrets out of the
# image. Its files are NAMED like real secrets -- deploy.pem, deploy.key,
# id_rsa, .aws/credentials -- and the fixture deletes them in a finally. This
# line covers the run that is killed before the finally: without it, the next
# `git add -A` stages two files called deploy.pem and deploy.key into a public
# repository, and nobody reads that diff twice.
#
# The path must match CONTEXT_PROBE_DIR in evals/hosted_docker/test_image.py,
# which the test compares against this rule, AND the tree must be one the tenant
# allowlist admits (hosted/image/tenant.Dockerfile.dockerignore). Both still say
# waku, so renaming this alone breaks the assertion.
waku/_c1_context_probe/

# The Word file the UI guide was generated FROM. It is 4 MB of screenshots that
# already live in the repo as Prometheus_Guide_images/*.png, so committing it
# doubles the image payload for nothing, and it is a source document rather
# than source code. Only the generated Markdown belongs here.
Prometheus_screenshots.docx
